# 6. Virtual File System (VFS)

Runtime assets are accessed through a Virtual File System rather than raw operating-system paths.

```text
Gameplay

↓

Asset Manager

↓

Virtual File System

↓

Package Archive

↓

Storage
```

The VFS abstracts the underlying storage medium.

Possible storage sources include:

* local archives,
* installed directories,
* downloadable content,
* cloud storage (future).

Subsystems remain unaware of physical storage details.

---

# 7. Package Archives

Runtime assets are grouped into package archives.

Examples:

```text
Base Content

Characters

Environment

Audio

Cinematics

Localization
```

Packaging related assets together improves loading performance and simplifies distribution.

---

# 8. Manifest Generation

Each release includes a package manifest.

Typical entries include:

* package identifier,
* asset identifiers,
* dependency information,
* version numbers,
* checksums,
* compression information.

The manifest provides a complete description of packaged content.

---

# 9. Asset References

Packaged assets continue to be referenced through the Asset System.

